    "details": "The rabbitmq-c project reports:\n\n> CVE-2026-61547: A heap buffer overflow exists when the\n> amqp_send_frame() API is used to serialise an oversized\n> AMQP_FRAME_BODY frame, as memcpy() writes past the end of the heap\n> allocation without validating that the body fragment fits within the\n> allocated frame buffer.\n>\n> CVE-2026-59986: An integer overflow in the amqp_decode_bytes bounds\n> check on 32-bit systems allows a malicious AMQP broker to craft frames\n> with oversized BYTES fields, resulting in an out-of-bounds read that\n> may expose process memory or crash the application.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0497",
